<title>FINLAND: VALMET SAYS WINS FIM 5 MLN SYSTEM ORDER.</title>
<headline>VALMET SAYS WINS FIM 5 MLN SYSTEM ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish paper machine maker Valmet Oy said on Thursday it had won an automation equipment order worth about five million markka from a subsidiary of Finnish forestry group Enso Oy .</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the deal is about five million markka,&quot; Valmet said in a statement.</p>
<p>Valmet said its automation unit would deliver a quality control and reporting system to the Kotka mill of Enso subsidiary Lamininating Papers Ltd for start-up in autumn 1997.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
